+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Current cycle: DOM identity defect
+
+The external Cypress acceptance suite reports five failures (tests 1-5). All trace to one root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and recreates every `<li>` from scratch on every state change. This destroys all DOM node references.
+
+**Affected acceptance-suite tests:**
+- "Mark all as completed" (tests 1, 2): clicking toggle-all or individual checkboxes triggers a full list rebuild; Cypress holds a stale `<li>` reference.
+- "Item" mark/unmark (tests 3, 4): same root cause on individual toggle.
+- "Routing - back button" (test 5): hashchange triggers `render()`, which rebuilds the list; the selector `.todo-list li:visible` finds nothing because nodes were destroyed and recreated.
+
+**Fix direction for Crew:** Mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place. When toggling a todo, find the existing `<li>` by `data-id`, toggle its `completed` class and checkbox `checked` attribute. When the filter changes, show/hide existing `<li>` elements rather than rebuilding. The `render()` function should reconcile existing nodes, not destroy and recreate them.
+
+**Specs planted:** `features/dom-identity.feature` (2 `@conformance` scenarios) and `features/hashchange-routing.feature` (1 `@conformance` scenario). These will fail on the current code because the step definitions for node-identity checks do not exist yet and, once authored, will expose the DOM replacement.
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` orders QM to target these three scenarios.
