+Feature: DOM identity preservation
+  As a user interacting with my todo list
+  I want the app to update existing elements in place
+  So that the browser retains element identity across state changes
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves the list-item DOM nodes
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | false     |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    Then each todo list-item node has a stable identity
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then each original todo list-item node is still in the DOM
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: Toggle-all preserves all list-item DOM nodes
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | false     |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    Then each todo list-item node has a stable identity
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then each original todo list-item node is still in the DOM
