+Feature: Hashchange-driven rendering
+  As a user navigating with browser controls
+  I want the todo list to update when the URL hash changes
+  So that the back and forward buttons work correctly
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Filtering by active shows only active todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | true      |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then only the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: Hashchange preserves list-item DOM nodes while re-rendering the filter
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | true      |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    Then each todo list-item node has a stable identity
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then each original todo list-item node is still in the DOM
